  "notes": "Sisters-harmony country-pop with dense, pop-arranged production. The tracking method is documented and is the reason the humanize is looser than the programming would suggest: drums were cut \"in the living room of the Bennett House (a converted historical home) for natural room character, then overdubbed at a big SSL room — so model a roomy, slightly loose kit under tight overdubs.\" Against that, \"shaker and tambourine 16ths are near-constant,\" which is the densest perc lane set in this batch. Harmony is the entry's real claim to distinctness: \"the most pop-functional in the 90s cohort — ii–V–I, IV–iv chromatic borrows and I–iii–IV–V,\" all three authored as families, with the IV–iv borrow the one that no other model in this section carries. The bass is quoted as \"mixed forward with pop-style syncopation (anticipations before the downbeat) rather than country root-fifth,\" so `followRootsProb` drops and `anticipationProb` goes to the top of this batch. Melody is \"syllabically busy with rhythmic hocketing between the three voices,\" hence the high density with a modest range. ⚠ Confidence is medium and the research says why: \"tracking method and tempo documented; harmonic specifics inferred from the lane [LOW-CONF].\" ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are the humanize values, the perc density and the countermelody ratio.",
